REGENT OF BALANGAN PROVINCE OF SOUTH KALIMANTAN
REGIONAL REGULATION OF BALANGAN REGENCY
NUMBER 3 OF 2016 CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
REGENT OF BALANGAN,

Considering: a. that every woman and child has the right to obtain protection of their human rights, freedom from torture, threats, pressure, as well as to receive equal facilities, treatment, opportunities and benefits in order to achieve justice and welfare of life;
b. that the improvement of the quality of life of women and children is a mandatory affair which is the responsibility of the Regional Government;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women From Acts of Violence;

In View of: 1. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection;
4. Law Number 2 of 2003 concerning Establishment of Tanah Bumbu Regency and Balangan Regency in the Province of South Kalimantan (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4265);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
7. Law Number 44 of 2008 concerning Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 181, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4928);
8. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
11. Presidential Regulation Number 18 of 2014 concerning Protection And Empowerment of Women And Children In Social Conflict (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 44);
12. Presidential Regulation Number 69 of 2008 concerning Task Force for Prevention and Handling of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 02 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Women's Protection;
14. Regulation of the Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2009 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons;
15. Regional Regulation of South Kalimantan Province Number 9 of 2008 concerning Protection of Neglected Children (Regional Gazette Year 2008 No.9);

With Mutual Approval

text:
BAB III RUANG LINGKUP
Pasa13 (1)Setiap perempuan dan anak berhak mendapatkan perlindungan dari tindak kekerasan.
(2)Tindak kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berupa tindakan:
a. kekerasan fisik;
b. kekerasan seksual;
c. kekerasan psikologis; d. intimidasi;
e. pengusiran paksa;
f. perampasan kemerdekaan; g. penelantaran; dan
h. eksploitasiy perdagangan orang.
(3)Perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan merupakan tanggungjawab bersama Pemerintah Daerah, masyarakat, keluarga, dan orang tua.
(4)Perlindungan perempuan dari tindak kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2)meliputi : a. pencegahan tindak kekerasan pada perempuan dan anak; b. pelayanan bagi perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan; dan
c. pemberdayaan perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III SCOPE
Article 13 (1) Every woman and child has the right to obtain protection from acts of violence.
(2) Acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) comprise actions of:
a. physical violence;
b. sexual violence;
c. psychological violence; d. intimidation;
e. forced eviction;
f. deprivation of liberty; g. neglect; and
h. exploitation and human trafficking.
(3) Protection of women and children from acts of violence is the joint responsibility of the Regional Government, community, family, and parents.
(4) Protection of women from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (2) includes: a. prevention of acts of violence against women and children; b. services for women and children victims of acts of violence; and
c. empowerment of women and children victims of acts of violence.

text:
BAB IV PENCEGAHAN
Pasal4 (1)Pemerintah Daerah, Masyarakat, Keluarga, dan Orang Tua berkewajiban untuk mencegah terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak untuk menghindari dampak situasi dan peristiwa.
(2)Pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) juga dilakukan terhadap: a. tindakan penelantaran; dan b. indikasi atau kegiatan yang mengandung potensi terjadinya perdagangan orang.
(3)Upaya pencegahan dilakukan dengan memperhatikan kondisi, situasi, permasalahan dan bentuk penanganan yang sesuai dan terarah.
Pasal5 (1)Pemerintah Daerah sesuai dengan kewenangan melakukan upaya pencegahan dini.
(2)Upaya pencegahan dini sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dalam bentuk:
a. melakukan pendataan dan pengkajian kondisi, pemenuhan hak dan berbagai aspek terkait dengan perempuan dan anak dalam kehidupan sosial di masyarakat;
b. memetakan wilayah rawan tindak kekerasan berdasarkan pendataan dan pengkajian sebagaimana dimaksud pada huruf a dan memberikan solusi bentuk/ cara yang mampu meminimalisasi kerawanan;
c. meningkatkan kesadaran hukum masyarakat melalui peran lembaga kemasyarakatan/pranata adat, forum komunikasi umat beragama untuk memberikan perlindungan perempuan dan anak;
d. meningkatkan peran media massa memberikan diseminasi dan informasi perlindungan perempuan dan anak;
e. penyuluhan atau sosialisasi peraturan perundang-undangan terkait dengan perlindungan perempuan dan anak secara rutin;
f. pembukaan jalur pengaduan masyarakat, dan jalur koordinasi dari tingkat desa Zkelurahan, kecamatan dan Pemerintah Daerah;
g. penanganan segera atas adanya laporan masyarakat.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IV PREVENTION
Article 4 (1) Regional Government, Community, Family, and Parents are obligated to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children to avoid the impact of situations and events.
(2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is also carried out against: a. acts of neglect; and b. indications or activities that contain the potential for occurrence of human trafficking.
(3) Prevention efforts are carried out by taking into account conditions, situations, problems and forms of handling that are appropriate and directed.
Article 5 (1) Regional Government in accordance with its authority carries out early prevention efforts.
(2) Early prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of:
a. conducting data collection and assessment of conditions, fulfillment of rights and various aspects related to women and children in social life in the community;
b. mapping areas vulnerable to acts of violence based on data collection and assessment as referred to in letter a and providing solutions in the form/manner capable of minimizing vulnerability;
c. increasing public legal awareness through the role of community institutions/customary institutions, interfaith communication forums to provide protection for women and children;
d. increasing the role of mass media in providing dissemination and information on protection of women and children;
e. counseling or socialization of laws and regulations related to protection of women and children on a regular basis;
f. opening channels for public complaints, and coordination channels from the village/kelurahan, sub-district and Regional Government levels;
g. immediate handling of community reports.

text:
BABVI PEMBERDAYAAN
Pasal8 (1) Pemerintah Daerah sesuai dengan kewenangan memberdayakan perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan dan penelantaran dalam bentuk meningkatkan ketahanan hidup dan meningkatkan usaha ekonomi.
(2) Meningkatkan ketahanan hidup sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dengan memberikan bimbingan dan pendampingan untuk penguatan mental spiritual berupa ilmu pengetahuan agama.
(3) Meningkatkan usaha ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dengan memberikan :
a.pelatihan keterampilan kerja;
b.pelatihan usaha ekonomi produktif dan kelompok usaha bersama;
c. pendampingan dalam pengembangan usaha ekonomi produktif;
d.bantuan permodalan; dan e.kemudahan akses informasi dan promosi pemasaran hasil produksi ekonomi produktif.
Pasa19 Anak korban kekerasan yang dicabut hak asuh orang tuanya terhadap pendidikannya menjadi tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah atau orang tua asuh yang mendapatkan hak asuh dari putusan pengadilan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VI EMPOWERMENT
Article 8 (1) The Regional Government in accordance with its authority shall empower women and children victims of violence and neglect in the form of improving life resilience and improving economic enterprises.
(2) Improving life resilience as referred to in paragraph (1) by providing guidance and assistance for mental spiritual strengthening in the form of religious knowledge.
(3) Improving economic enterprises as referred to in paragraph (1) by providing:
a. job skills training;
b. productive economic enterprise training and joint business groups;
c. assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;
d. capital assistance; and e. ease of access to information and marketing promotion of productive economic production results.
Article 9 Child victims of violence whose parental custody rights have been revoked, their education becomes the responsibility of the Regional Government or foster parents who obtain custody rights from a court decision.

text:
BAB VIII PERAN SERTA MASYARAKAT
Pasal18 (1)Masyarakat dapat berperan serta memberikan perlindungan dan pemberdayaan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasaan, penelantaran dan perdagangan orang.
(2)Peran serta masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat berupa:
a. memberikan informasi kepada pejabat atau lembaga yang berwenang;
b. membantu penyelamatan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
c. memberikan bantuan kebutuhan dasar dan atau spesifik bagi perempuan dan anak;
d. membentuk mitra keluarga atau unit kecil dilingkungan desa/kelurahan yang aktif secara bersama menjaga lingkungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
e. mensosialisasikan hak perempuan dan anak secara mandiri;
f. memberikan bantuan hukum dan pendampingan.
(3)Peran serta masyarakat dalam memberikan perlindungan dan pemberdayaan perempuan dan anak dilaksanakan secara bertanggungjawab sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang- undangan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VIII COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 18 (1) The community can participate in providing protection and empowerment to women and children victims of violence, neglect and human trafficking.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of:
a. providing information to authorized officials or institutions;
b. assisting in the rescue of women and children;
c. providing basic and or specific needs assistance for women and children;
d. forming family partners or small units at the village/sub-district level that actively work together to protect the environment of women and children from acts of violence;
e. independently socializing the rights of women and children;
f. providing legal assistance and accompaniment.
(3) Community participation in providing protection and empowerment of women and children shall be carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
